      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: Instead of overwriting the reset flags with `EC_RESET_FLAG_HIBERNATE` and then clearing them with `0`, it would be safer to read the existing flags, add `EC_RESET_FLAG_HIBERNATE`, and then restore them if `board_hibernate_late()` returns. \n\n`chip_save_reset_flags()` overwrites the entire value in BBRAM. This means that if `CONFIG_POWER_BUTTON_INIT_IDLE` is enabled, `EC_RESET_FLAG_AP_IDLE` might be present in the saved flags and will be lost.\n\nConsider doing this instead:\n```c\n\t\tuint32_t saved_flags \u003d chip_read_reset_flags();\n\t\tchip_save_reset_flags(saved_flags | EC_RESET_FLAG_HIBERNATE);\n\t\tboard_hibernate_late();\n\t\tchip_save_reset_flags(saved_flags);\n```",
